'''Soportújar New Town''' ({{Lang-bl|Ciudad Nueva de Soportújar}}) is a [[Planned communities in Balisca|planned community]] in the [[Coruxón]] borough of the [[Castejón|Castejón Metropolis]]. ''Soportújar'' ({{Literal translation|place of the {{W|arcade (architecture)|arcades}}}}) takes it's name from the presence of major shopping centers ("arcades") for various [[W:Consumer goods|consumer goods]], household electronics and the [[W:Black market|black market]].

It was developed to encourage [[W:Affordable housing|affordable housing]] and [[W:Transit-oriented development|urban decentralization]], which was significantly aided by the opening of [[Soportújar Station]] in 1986. Soportújar has experienced phenomenal growth since 1992, usually drawing in younger generations of both naturally-born Baliscans and immigrant communities.

Soportújar's population is 148,347 as of 2024. It is served by the [[Castejón Metro Soportújar Line|Soportújar Line]] of the [[Castejón Metro]].
